    "**Answer 2 (Task A — spam):**\n",
    "_(A model here would sit in front of an inbox and decide, per message, whether to route it to spam or the main folder — that's the \"decision\" it supports. It's binary because a message is either unwanted (spam) or legitimate (ham); there's no third bucket.)_\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer 2 (Task B — sentiment):**\n",
    "_(This model would let an airline automatically scan tweets mentioning them and flag negative ones for a support team to review first. It's binary once neutral tweets are excluded, since only \"happy customer\" vs. \"unhappy customer\" remain as targets.)_"
   ]
