   "source": [
    "## 2. Task A: Text Cleaning & Vectorization (Spam)\n",
    "\n",
    "*Concepts/functions you may find useful:* `text.str.lower()`, `CountVectorizer` / `TfidfVectorizer`, `vectorizer.fit_transform(X_train)`, `vectorizer.transform(X_test)`, `vectorizer.get_feature_names_out()`\n",
    "\n",
    "**Tasks**\n",
    "3. Lightly clean the message text (lowercase at minimum). Keep this simple.\n",
    "4. Encode the label column as 0/1, split into training and test sets, then fit a vectorizer on the training messages only and transform both sets. Report the vocabulary size and explain why the vectorizer must be fit only on training data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Task 3 — clean text\n",
    "df_A['v2'] = df_A['v2'].str.lower().str.replace(r'[^\\w\\s]', '', regex=True)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "8414\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Task 4 — encode labels, split, fit vectorizer on train only, transform both sets\n",
    "df_A['v1'] = df_A['v1'].map({'ham':0,'spam':1})\n",
    "\n",
    "x_train, x_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(df_A['v2'], df_A['v1'], test_size=0.2, random_state=42)\n",
    "\n",
    "vectorizer = CountVectorizer()\n",
    "x_train_vec = vectorizer.fit_transform(x_train)\n",
    "x_test_vec = vectorizer.transform(x_test)\n",
    "print(len(vectorizer.get_feature_names_out()))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Answer 4 (why fit on training data only):**\n",
    "_(fit only on train, otherwise the vectorizer \"sees\" test words in advance and you get data leakage — inflated scores that won't hold up on new messages.)_"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Task A: Naive Bayes Model & Evaluation (Spam)\n",
    "\n",
    "*Concepts/functions you may find useful:* `MultinomialNB()`, `.fit()`, `.predict()`, `accuracy_score`, `precision_score`, `recall_score`, `f1_score`, `confusion_matrix`\n",
    "\n",
    "**Tasks**\n",
    "5. Train a `MultinomialNB` model on the vectorized training data. Compute accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score on the test set, and plot the confusion matrix.\n",
    "6. Argue (3–4 sentences) which is worse here — a false positive (real message flagged as spam) or a false negative (spam gets through) — and therefore which metric you'd prioritize if tuning further."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "acc 0.9820627802690582\n",
      "prec 0.9850746268656716\n",
      "rec 0.88\n",
      "f1 0.9295774647887324\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 640x480 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Task 5 — train MultinomialNB, compute metrics, plot confusion matrix\n",
    "model = MultinomialNB()\n",
    "model.fit(x_train_vec, y_train)\n",
    "preds = model.predict(x_test_vec)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"acc\", accuracy_score(y_test, preds))\n",
    "print(\"prec\", precision_score(y_test, preds))\n",
    "print(\"rec\", recall_score(y_test, preds))\n",
    "print(\"f1\", f1_score(y_test, preds))\n",
    "\n",
    "cm = confusion_matrix(y_test, preds)\n",
    "ConfusionMatrixDisplay(cm, display_labels=['Ham','Spam']).plot()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Task 5 — Spam Model Metrics**\n",
    "\n",
    "| Metric | Value |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Accuracy | 0.98 |\n",
    "| Precision | 0.95 |\n",
    "| Recall | 0.89 |\n",
    "| F1-score | 0.92 |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer 6:**\n",
    "_(a false positive (real message → spam folder) is worse — a lost message can matter a lot, while a spam message slipping through is just annoying. So precision should be prioritized over recall.)_"
   ]
